#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:1
msgid "RFC-0003: Hypervisor Support"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:3
msgid "Status: Approved"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:4
msgid "Pull request: https://github.com/asterinas/asterinas/pull/3418"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:5
msgid "Date submitted: 2026-06-21"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:6
msgid "Date approved: 2026-08-05"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:8
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:10
msgid ""
"This RFC proposes extending OSTD with hypervisor support. These OSTD "
"facilities allow the Asterinas kernel to safely implement a complete "
"hypervisor, including a KVM-compatible control plane, while keeping "
"privileged virtualization mechanisms inside OSTD."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:12
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:14
msgid ""
"Asterinas needs virtualization support for existing Linux KVM-based VMMs and "
"unmodified guest kernels."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:16
msgid ""
"Supporting virtualization requires extending the framekernel boundary with "
"care. Taking x86 as an example, a malformed VMCS, a bad EPT mapping, or an "
"incorrectly restored host register can break the soundness semantics of the "
"host kernel. Therefore, this RFC focuses on what kind of OSTD hypervisor "
"layer Asterinas needs: it must provide soundness by encapsulating privileged "
"virtualization mechanisms, minimality by keeping the trusted surface small, "
"and expressiveness by giving the Asterinas kernel enough safe operations to "
"build a complete hypervisor above it."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:18
msgid "Design"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:20
msgid "Layering"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:22
msgid ""
"This split of the virtualization mechanism and the policy mirrors the "
"existing user-mode design in Asterinas. The kernel can decide what to run "
"and how to handle exits, but the transition that could affect host CPU state "
"is mediated by OSTD."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:24
msgid ""
"The Asterinas kernel owns the KVM-compatible file-descriptor ABI and kernel "
"policy. It implements `/dev/kvm`, VM file descriptors, vCPU file "
"descriptors, the `kvm_run` shared page, memory-slot registration, register "
"ioctls, basic in-kernel irqchip emulation, and conversion between KVM "
"structs and OSTD types."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:26
msgid ""
"OSTD owns the virtualization mechanism. It manages hardware virtualization "
"state, second-stage address translation, and guest-host context switching, "
"and returns `GuestRunResult` events to the kernel. The VM-exit case carries "
"a small `GuestExitInfo` record."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:28
msgid "OSTD Interface Design"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:30
msgid ""
"OSTD provides three new abstractions. `GuestPhysMemSpace` represents guest "
"physical memory and owns second-stage translation from guest physical "
"addresses to host frames. `GuestContext` represents the per-vCPU "
"architectural state that must survive across guest exits. `GuestMode` is the "
"execution object that enters guest mode, handles the guest-host state "
"transition, and returns exits to the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:32
msgid ""
"The following diagram shows the core object ownership and the upper-lower "
"relationship between the kernel hypervisor layer and the OSTD VM API."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:34
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TB\n"
"    subgraph KF[\"kernel fd objects\"]\n"
"        direction LR\n"
"        VmFile[\"VmFile<br/>VM fd\"]\n"
"        VcpuFile[\"VcpuFile<br/>vCPU fd\"]\n"
"    end\n"
"\n"
"    subgraph KS[\"kernel VM/vCPU state\"]\n"
"        direction LR\n"
"        Vm[\"Vm<br/>memory slots\"]\n"
"        Vcpu[\"Vcpu<br/>per-vCPU state\"]\n"
"        Policy[\"interrupt and timer policy\"]\n"
"    end\n"
"\n"
"    subgraph O[\"ostd safe public API\"]\n"
"        direction LR\n"
"        Gpm[\"GuestPhysMemSpace\"]\n"
"        Context[\"GuestContext\"]\n"
"        Mode[\"GuestMode::execute\"]\n"
"        Ports[\"GuestInterruptPort<br/>GuestTimerPort\"]\n"
"    end\n"
"\n"
"    VmFile -- \"own (Arc)\" --> Vm\n"
"    VmFile -- \"KVM_CREATE_VCPU\" --> VcpuFile\n"
"    VcpuFile -- \"own (Arc)\" --> Vm\n"
"    VcpuFile -- \"own (Arc)\" --> Vcpu\n"
"\n"
"    Vm -- \"own (by value)\" --> Gpm\n"
"    Vm -- \"own vCPU table (Arc)\" --> Vcpu\n"
"\n"
"    Vcpu -- \"borrow (Weak)\" --> Vm\n"
"    Vcpu -- \"own (Mutex)\" --> Context\n"
"    Vcpu -- \"own\" --> Mode\n"
"    Vcpu -- \"own\" --> Policy\n"
"\n"
"    Policy -. \"implements\" .-> Ports\n"
"    Mode -- \"borrow\" --> Ports\n"
"    Mode -- \"borrow\" --> Gpm\n"
"    Mode -- \"mutable borrow\" --> Context\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

