#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:196
#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:373
msgid "**Soundness.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:198
msgid ""
"`GuestContext` merely wraps the vCPU state and provides interfaces for "
"reading and setting the vCPU state. Through these interfaces, it does not "
"affect the host state, nor does it impact the memory safety of the host "
"kernel."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:200
#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:379
msgid "**Minimality.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:202
msgid ""
"`GuestContext` centralizes the vCPU data that OSTD must understand when "
"switching into guest mode. To the kernel, it is a minimal vCPU state "
"interface for configuring and running a guest. Additional device-level vCPU "
"state, such as irqchip state, remains in the kernel or userspace VMM layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:204
#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:383
msgid "**Expressiveness.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:206
msgid ""
"`GuestContext` exposes enough interfaces for the kernel to configure key "
"guest registers such as general-purpose registers, system registers and so "
"on. This lets the kernel build vCPUs in various states, and update guest "
"state while emulating exits such as MMIO accesses."
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:208
msgid "GuestMode"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:210
msgid ""
"`GuestMode` is the OSTD execution object that performs VM entry and returns "
"VM exits. The public interfaces are:"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:213
msgid "// ostd/src/vm/mod.rs\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md:214
msgid ""
"/// Runs guest vCPU code in an isolated guest execution mode.\n"
"///\n"
"/// `GuestMode` is the OSTD-side execution object for a guest vCPU. It "
"enters\n"
"/// guest execution with the vCPU context and kernel-provided policy ports\n"
"/// supplied to [`Self::execute`] until a VM exit must be handled outside "
"OSTD.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Examples\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```no_run\n"
"/// # fn handle_vm_exit(guest_result: ostd::vm::GuestRunResult) {}\n"
"/// #\n"
"/// use ostd::{\n"
"///     arch::vm::GuestContext,\n"
"///     prelude::*,\n"
"///     vm::{GuestInterruptPort, GuestMode, GuestPhysMemSpace, "
"GuestTimerPort},\n"
"/// };\n"
"///\n"
"/// fn run_guest(\n"
"///     context: &mut GuestContext,\n"
"///     interrupt_port: &dyn GuestInterruptPort,\n"
"///     timer_port: &dyn GuestTimerPort,\n"
"///     guest_mem: &GuestPhysMemSpace,\n"
"/// ) -> Result<()> {\n"
"///     let guest_mode = GuestMode::new()?;\n"
"///\n"
"///     loop {\n"
"///         let run_result = guest_mode.execute(context, guest_mem, "
"interrupt_port, timer_port)?;\n"
"///         // Handle VM exit according to the exit reason recorded in "
"`run_result`.\n"
"///         handle_vm_exit(run_result);\n"
"///     }\n"
"/// }\n"
"/// ```\n"
msgstr ""

